{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/82280-an-idea-for-an-idea-for-an-npc-pantheon-for-my-upcoming-game","id":82280,"title":"An idea for an idea for an NPC Pantheon for my upcoming game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-01T13:38:18-08:00","id":82280,"title":"An idea for an idea for an NPC Pantheon for my upcoming game","content":"Deno, Vera, Caitlin, don't read this thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm currently in the planning stages for a Scion campaign for my group that will be a sequel to one that another storyteller in my group is currently running. The plan is to be the scions of the player characters from the current game. The current game is steeped heavily in Ragnarok. As such we attempted to save as many Aesir from their appointed deaths. In order to save Loki and Heimdall from killing one another, one of the other players created a robotic Loki to take the place of Loki during Ragnarok. Loki was pleased by this misdirection. <br /> <br /> The Lokibot was never supposed to know it was a machine, but it didn't have the hardware to take on Heimdall. But the player who made the Lokibot got a frankly disgustingly awesome roll in it's creation process. So I'm thinking, what if the Lokibot was clever enough to realize that he was a machine? What if then the Lokibot created a second Lokibot to then take his place against Heimdall. <br /> <br /> For my sequel, my goal is to make this Lokibot a major antagonist. Therefore I'm thinking that perhaps he, although made of metal and silicone, was somehow a scion of the god who created him. And then went on to attain godhood himself. I'm thinking of a Machine God Pantheon for my game. But right now it is just an idea for an idea. So I thought I would post here and see if anyone else can offer any other suggestions or feedback for this idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T13:54:00-08:00","id":82290,"title":"","content":"I forgot to mention that the current game we are playing in takes place around 1929. So my sequel will take place in modern times. So other than the Lokibot, the only ideas I have so far is a god of information/internet and a god of the atom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T07:08:18-08:00","id":82608,"title":"","content":"Hm. Well, it's certainly an interesting idea. Where are the rest of these gods coming from, anyway? Is the &quot;Lokibot&quot; building them? I suggest looking at fictional portrayals of robots/AI for inspiration. And don't limit yourself just to deity concepts based around the &quot;information age.&quot; For example, R. Daneel Olivaw would be an interesting basis for a god of justice. HAL 9000 could offer an interesting take on a god of truth. If you're in the mood for something light, Bender would be amusing as a god of pleasure or self-interest (or even a straight up god of alcohol, I suppose). I could see Data forming the basis for a god of self-improvement and personal achievement. Gort could be a counter-intuitive approach to a God of Peace. Anyway, if you want to go with this concept, there is a lot of good science fiction out there to draw inspiration from. Just don't forget the fembots. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T10:10:53-08:00","id":82677,"title":"","content":"Yes, I figured they would all be scions of the Lokibot. (whom I need to give a better name to) Either one's that he built himself, or creations of mankind whom he felt worthy enough to improve and adopt into his fold. But your ideas do have me thinking, thank you for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T13:27:55-08:00","id":82755,"title":"","content":"An idea: The Lokibot could have made a copy of its awareness, that can slowly rebuild itself during your new story. SO instead of being a full-on god, it is a divine level artificial intelligence with thousands of copies scattered across the Overworld, the Underworld and Earth. Each seed is building a new form and body. The materials available are being used. So several Heros are emerging on Earth (Bell, Tesla, Einstein could be heroes of Lokibot), A handful of demigods in the underworld. And your main pantheon of gods in the overworld. OF course the remains of the Lokibot (which appeared destroyed, is actually designed to look this way and has been a Fully Operational Lokibot for years - why could no one detect its power - it was jamming them...) The Lokibot could have orchestrated its prime directive of protecting Loki's life. This will mean putting Koki in a boring safe place... which may eventually turn Koki against the lokibot... or not.<br /> <br /> Now I may have to steal this for myself...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T14:16:40-08:00","id":82779,"title":"","content":"Hm, I may have to use that Gideon, or at least mine some of it for ideas.<br /> <br /> I guess a little more background on what else is going to go down in my campaign could help with the idea process also. After the events in Ragnarok, many people are aware of the existence of gods, though not everyone uses that term for them. At one point during our current campaign, the Jormungandr Serpent wrapped itself around the entirety of Japan. Not to mention my current character (a scion of Tyr) gained a cult following of people dedicated to her cause of helping the unfortunate in the San Francisco arctic wasteland (Yeah, Fimbulvinter) <br /> <br /> So now in the sequel campaign it's modern day. The world is coping with over half of its population being lost during the &quot;ice age&quot; it went through. The political landscape is vastly different. During the winter most governments lost their ability to govern their nations. Towns during Fimbulvinter became their own entities that were wholly interested only in their own survival. Some towns became raiders, pillaging their neighbors for supplies. So after the big thaw, not everyone was interested in going back under the rule of someone who helped them absolutely zero. To boot many organizations were claiming to be the one true American government in the states. After some scuffles, then a war, the country is again Divided into the North and South. The north being the New United States, and the south being The Confederate Union of states.<br /> <br /> The players in my sequel campaign are citizens of the NUS. But there is an organization in the NUS who is trying to suppress knowledge of gods and titans. They call themselves Task Force Prometheus. Using technology devised from the fire of Prometheus, they are trying to protect mankind from having to suffer the fate of another Ragnarok. They intend to put a field over the entire planet which will prevent Gods from manifesting on the Earth plane. But what they don't know is that their organization has been hijacked by the Machine Gods. The Prometheus field doesn't affect the Machine Gods.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I haven't really pinned down the Machine Gods' motivation. I'm thinking they think that they can stop the titans through sheer order, but perhaps even their strings are being pulled by some unknown Titan whom I'll have to conceive of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2412-lucidfeverdream","name":"LucidFeverDream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}